reviews.body:
### Blocking Issues

  1. `events.js` not updated — functional regression

  `events.js:597–603` detects tab switches by matching `[onclick*="Admin.showTab"]`:
```bash
  document.addEventListener("click", function (event) {
    if (
      event.target.matches('[onclick*="Admin.showTab"]') ||
      event.target.closest('[onclick*="Admin.showTab"]')
    ) {
      resetSearchInputsState();
      initializeSearchInputsDebounced();
    }
  });
```

  The PR removes all `onclick="Admin.showTab('...')"` attributes from nav links, so this handler never fires. Search state will no longer reset on tab switch. This file was not modified in the PR and needs to be updated — e.g. match on `.sidebar-link` instead.

  2. Stale guard and comment in `initialization.js:258–262`

```bash
  // The sidebar anchors already have inline onclick handlers in admin.html.
  // Avoid adding a second click handler that would call showTab twice.
  if (tabElement.hasAttribute("onclick")) {
    return;
  }
```

  Since onclick attributes are gone, this guard is now dead code. All tabs now fall through to `tabElement.addEventListener("click", () => showTab(tabName))` — which is correct for navigation, but the stale comment and dead guard should be removed.

3. No integration test for `nonce` header ↔ template consistency

  The tests verify that the helper function returns the right value, and the CSP header structure looks correct. The most important invariant — that the nonce embedded in `<script nonce="...">` tags in rendered HTML matches the nonce in the `Content-Security-Policy` header — is not tested. A Playwright or integration test hitting an admin page and comparing both would catch any future regression.
